{# polysource/easyadmin-filter-bridge — override of @EasyAdmin/crud/index.html.twig

   Injects an "active filters" chips bar above the table on EA index
   pages. Each chip displays the property name (humanised) and an X
   button that strips that filter slice from the URL via the
   `polysource--filter-chips` Stimulus controller (shipped with
   `polysource/filter`).

   Why this is the right extension point:
   - EA's filter modal renders inside a Bootstrap dialog and only
     surfaces the operator/value form. There's no upstream surface
     that lists "what's currently applied" outside the modal — users
     have to open the modal to see what's filtered, which is poor
     scanning UX on lists with many columns.
   - The chips bar gives users an at-a-glance summary without
     reopening the modal, plus one-click removal per filter.

   Strict additivity:
   - We only override the `main` block to prepend the chips bar
     before delegating to the upstream block via `parent()`. Every
     other EA block (page actions, table head, paginator, …)
     remains untouched.
   - The chips bar is hidden when no filters are applied (CSS
     handled by Bootstrap's `d-none`-on-empty pattern via Twig
     `{% if applied_filters %}` guard).

   Why `@!EasyAdmin/...`:
   - Symfony's Twig namespace resolution finds OUR copy of
     `crud/index.html.twig` first (since DI prepends our views to
     the `@EasyAdmin` namespace). The bang-prefix `@!EasyAdmin`
     skips that resolution and reaches the original upstream file
     directly, preventing an infinite extends loop.
#}
{% extends '@!EasyAdmin/crud/index.html.twig' %}

{% block main %}
    {% set applied_filters = ea.request.query.all['filters']|default([]) %}
    {% if applied_filters|length > 0 %}
        <div class="polysource-filter-chips-bar mb-3"
             data-controller="polysource--filter-chips">
            <span class="text-muted me-2">{{ 'polysource.filter.chips.heading'|trans({}, 'PolysourceEasyAdminFilterBridge') }}</span>
            {% for property, _ in applied_filters %}
                <span class="badge bg-secondary me-1 polysource-filter-chip"
                      data-polysource--filter-chips-target="chip"
                      data-property="{{ property }}">
                    {{ property|replace({'_': ' '})|capitalize }}
                    <button type="button"
                            class="btn-close btn-close-white ms-1"
                            aria-label="{{ 'polysource.filter.chips.remove'|trans({}, 'PolysourceEasyAdminFilterBridge') }}"
                            data-action="click->polysource--filter-chips#removeChip"
                            data-polysource--filter-chips-property-param="{{ property }}"></button>
                </span>
            {% endfor %}
            <a href="{{ ea_url().unset('filters').setAction('index') }}"
               class="btn btn-link btn-sm polysource-filter-chips-clear-all">
                {{ 'polysource.filter.chips.clear_all'|trans({}, 'PolysourceEasyAdminFilterBridge') }}
            </a>
        </div>
    {% endif %}

    {{ parent() }}
{% endblock main %}
